  "interpretation": [
    "A real 5-second TWDT idle-progress failure occurred; the collector detects the literal diagnostic correctly. It should be distinguished from MFAULT, but distinction does not make this run pass.",
    "PANIC is disabled in the matching image configuration; IDF task_wdt_timeout_handling prints a backtrace and returns in this case. Continued same-session frames and successful CAP8/USB recovery are consistent with non-reset behavior.",
    "The interrupted stack is within the Bluetooth controller scheduler. This is an interrupt-time snapshot, not proof that btController alone continuously monopolized CPU0 for the full interval. Other Core0 tasks and scheduling/bus pressure remain unisolated.",
    "USB whole-record drops, partial writes and timeouts grew before and after the watchdog; BLE data-drop counters also grew. An absence of BLE fragmentError is not proof of peer delivery or scheduling health.",
    "ESP_EARLY_LOGE in LOG_VERSION_1 uses esp_rom_printf from the watchdog ISR, bypassing the application SerialIo record queue. The observed emergency diagnostic splits a scientific header. This is not evidence that stdioBound regressed or that ordinary queued control/data writers gained a second owner.",
    "Only 15.065057333995355 seconds of the requested 120-second capture completed. The 16 complete CRC-valid USB frames cannot establish a 120-second stability/FPS result.",
    "No physical-safety conclusion follows from a non-reset watchdog or successful recovery query."
  ],
